    "created_at": "2023-09-03T12:55:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-03T18:26:48Z",
    "body": "as that particular bit is explicitly about \"If the element is an [input](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#the-input-element) element that **does not** [represent](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#represents) an image\", the use of \"alternative text\" is unnecessarily confusing. I think it should say \"accessible name\" (which then covers the other things mentioned, like 'title')\r\n\r\n> If the element is an [input](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#the-input-element) element that does not [represent](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#represents) an image and the user agent does not expect this to change\r\n> The user agent is expected to treat the element as a [replaced element](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display/#replaced-element) consisting of a button whose content is the element's **[accessible name](https://www.w3.org/TR/accname/)**. The [natural dimensions](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#natural-dimensions) of the button are expected to be about one line in height and whatever width is necessary to render the text on one line.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
