    "created_at": "2023-09-03T17:09:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-03T17:09:34Z",
    "body": "I don't think it should be accessible name. HTML shouldn't depend on ARIA in that way. But it should be more clear, agreed. The questions here are:\r\n\r\n1. Do we want alt -> title -> value or some other combination of attributes?\r\n2. What should we do if we end up with an empty string, given that it's a button and likely not just decorative?\r\n3. Should we render a broken image icon as Chromium appears to do?\r\n4. Are we constrained somehow by web compatibility?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
