    "created_at": "2023-09-03T18:52:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-03T18:52:16Z",
    "body": "1. I'd say `alt` -> `title` -> value would make sense\r\n2./3. Explicitly falling back to \"Submit\" may make sense / be more user-friendly than showing a broken image with no text alternative/accName. It does skirt a bit towards browsers applying error-correction of sorts though\r\n4. I'd hazard a guess (not sure if there's an appropriate counter somewhere for it) that `<input type=\"image\">` usage is relatively low - would be good to get some sense of this\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
